OL,3,GNEWSAThe school hit by a wartime bomber
OL,4,Athat was on its way home
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt was the early hours of a July
OL,7,Fmorning in 1941 and a Hampden bomber
OL,8,Fwas returning to RAF Waddington in
OL,9,FLincolnshire after an operation off the
OL,10,Fnorth coast of the Netherlands. It
OL,11,Fnever made it home.
OL,13,FThe aircraft, which was registered as
OL,14,FAD943 and was part of 44 Squadron, is
OL,15,Fbelieved to have suffered a mechanical
OL,16,Ffailure just five miles (8km) from the
OL,17,Fairbase.
OL,19,FIt crashed into the staff accommodation
OL,20,Fblock of Lincoln Christ's Hospital
OL,21,FGirls' High School, which stood on the
OL,22,F12th Century Greestone Stairs.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
